{"key":"bipartite-coloring-e0500cee2d656db8","sourceHash":"e0500cee2d656db88c5dc510d004ac5893edcd1550ce29a8526363fbebd6e561","pattern":"bipartite-coloring","category":"graph-traversal","title":"Bipartite Coloring: Mental Model","idea":"Assign opposite colors across every edge and reject any edge whose endpoints match.","complexity":"O(V+E) time · O(V) space","source":"fn bipartite(graph: &[Vec<usize>]) -> bool {\n    let mut color = vec![None; graph.len()];\n    for start in 0..graph.len() {\n        if color[start].is_some() {\n            continue;\n        }\n        color[start] = Some(false);\n        let mut queue = std::collections::VecDeque::from([start]);\n        while let Some(v) = queue.pop_front() {\n            for &u in &graph[v] {\n                if color[u] == color[v] {\n                    return false;\n                }\n                if color[u].is_none() {\n                    color[u] = Some(!color[v].unwrap());\n                    queue.push_back(u);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    true\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let result = bipartite(&[vec![1, 3], vec![0, 2], vec![1, 3], vec![0, 2]]).to_string();\n    println!(\"{result}\");\n}\n","sites":[{"line":2,"function":"bipartite","statement":"let mut color = vec![None; graph.len()];"},{"line":3,"function":"bipartite","statement":"for start in 0..graph.len() {"},{"line":4,"function":"bipartite","statement":"if color[start].is_some() {"},{"line":5,"function":"bipartite","statement":"continue;"},{"line":7,"function":"bipartite","statement":"color[start] = Some(false);"},{"line":8,"function":"bipartite","statement":"let mut queue = std::collections::VecDeque::from([start]);"},{"line":9,"function":"bipartite","statement":"while let Some(v) = queue.pop_front() {"},{"line":10,"function":"bipartite","statement":"for &u in &graph[v] {"},{"line":11,"function":"bipartite","statement":"if color[u] == color[v] {","edge":{"collection":"graph","from":"v","to":"u"}},{"line":12,"function":